speechtext:
I have the honour to inform the House that a message has been received from the Senate informing this House that the Senate has passed the following Bills, without amendment:
Bill C-88, an Act to authorize the acquisition of Marine Atlantic Inc. and to provide for other matters in relation thereto;
Bill C-96, an Act to amend the Federal-Provincial Fiscal Arrangements and Federal Post-Secondary Education and Health Contributions Act, 1977;
Bill C- 111, an Act to amend the Customs Tariff and to amend An Act to amend the Customs Tariff;
Bill C-112, an Act to amend the Energy Administration Act and provide for certain matters in relation thereto;
Bill C-116, an Act to amend the Canada Pension Plan and the Federal Court Act;
Bill C-117, an Act to facilitate financial arrangements between farmers and their creditors;
Bill C-128, an Act to amend the Judges Act and other Acts in relation to judicial matters;
Bill C-90, an Act respecting pension plans organized and administered for the benefit of persons employed in connection with certain federal works, undertakings and businesses;
